.SH "NAME"
pam_postgresok \- PAM module to simple check of real UID and corresponding account name
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.HP \w'\fBpam_postgresok\&.so\fR\ 'u
\fBpam_postgresok\&.so\fR [debug]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
pam_postgresok\&.so is designed to check that the real UID of the calling process belongs to the "postgres" user and equal to 26 (the value assigned to that user on Red Hat Linux systems)\&.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.PP
debug
.RS 4
Write debugging messages to syslog\&.
.RE
.SH "MODULE TYPES PROVIDED"
.PP
Only
\fBauth\fR
module type is provided\&.
.SH "RETURN VALUES"
.PP
.PP
PAM_SUCCESS
.RS 4
Everything was successful\&.
.RE
.PP
PAM_AUTH_ERR
.RS 4
Authentication failed\&.
.RE
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
    auth sufficient pam_postgresok\&.so
      
.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
